 "W1_rule": "D7 step (1), for each missed column entry [lo, hi] with the failed call's mass residuals r(lo), r(hi) as evidence: if r(lo) > 0 and r(hi) > 0 (root below lo): lo -> template_lo if lo > template_lo else lo/2; if r(lo) < 0 and r(hi) < 0 (root above hi): hi -> 1.05*template_hi if hi < 1.05*template_hi else 2*hi; the other end is kept. fs template = [1.5125e8, 3.025e8] (driver v001 solver template DDO154_REMAINING_FREE_SURFACE_CONTROLS_V001 5d69360f); for rfs/le factor entries the template is the rule factor pair of that pass (rfs_factors; le_first_factors for pass 1, le_next_factors after). The hull [template_lo, 1.05*template_hi] = [1.5125e8, 3.17625e8] contains the template and every inherited override and equals the reviewed NGC fs bracket [h0/2, 1.05 h0] (v005 CHECK_V001, N4).",
 "step4_text": "D7 step (4) is applied as written: EVERY case is compared with the R1 block (gate V3, \"the D7 recovery block, as a whole, for every case\"). Completed or running cases are rerun admitting their own prefixes: C2 -> C2R (v001, admits F10 route-A/reference/body, passes 6); C3, C4, R (v005, running with the anchor block) -> C3R, C4R, RR admitting their own v005 prefixes once those exist; S3, Y3, S4, Y4 are generated with R1 from the start. The first attempts stay on record.",
 "later_invocations": "The same rule applies to any later column-pass bracket miss in any case (S3, Y3, S4, Y4 included): R(n) = R(n-1) with only the newly missed entries widened by W1 from that failed call's evidence; every case is regenerated with R(n) (completed cases rerun admitting their own prefixes); the comparison takes --bracket-recovery R(n). The compare script refuses a recovery block that changes anything but override entries, narrows or removes any anchor entry, or does not contain every R1 entry. A column that misses again after a W1 step B widening is reported BRACKET_RECOVERY_EXHAUSTED for review (matrix INCOMPLETE). A miss of type \"no bracket source\" is outside W1 and is reported for review.",
